            <ArticleTitle>Sacroiliac syndrome associated with lumbosacral anomalies: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>171-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A successfully treated case of sacroiliac syndrome coexisting with lumbosacral anomalies is presented. Spinal manipulative therapy is not contraindicated if properly modified to account for the anomalous anatomical orientation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
